---
import Base from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';import CTA from '../../components/CTA.astro';import {products} from '../../data/products';
---
<Base title="Fiber Optic Temperature Sensors & Systems | INNO" description="Compare INNO fluorescent point probes, multi-channel monitors, transformer systems and OEM modules by measurement task and integration requirements."><section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Product portfolio</p><h1>Fiber Optic Temperature Sensors and Measurement Systems</h1><p>Choose a fluorescent point probe for the measurement location, then match it to a compatible monitor or OEM module. A complete system also needs optical routing, channel mapping and the required control interface.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container grid">{products.map(p=><article class="card linked-card product-card">{p.image&&<a class="product-image-link" href={`/products/${p.slug}/`} aria-label={`View ${p.name}`}><img src={p.image} alt={`${p.name} product image`} loading="lazy"></a>}<p class="eyebrow">{p.category}</p><h2><a href={`/products/${p.slug}/`}>{p.name}</a></h2><p>{p.summary}</p></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="section tint"><div class="container prose">
  <h2>Choose a product family by measurement task</h2>
  <table class="spec"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Your task</th><th scope="col">Product family to review</th><th scope="col">Confirm before selection</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">Measure a local contact temperature</th><td><a href="/products/fluorescent-fiber-optic-temperature-probe/">Fluorescent probes</a></td><td>Tip geometry, thermal contact, materials and optical route.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Read multiple optical points</th><td><a href="/products/multi-channel-fiber-optic-temperature-monitor/">Multi-channel monitors</a></td><td>Probe compatibility, channel count, diagnostics and supported outputs.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Plan a transformer winding system</th><td><a href="/products/transformer-fiber-optic-temperature-sensor/">Transformer probe-and-monitor systems</a></td><td>Approved winding points, installation stage and controls integration.</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Integrate sensing into OEM equipment</th><td><a href="/products/fiber-optic-temperature-sensing-module/">IF-G sensing module</a></td><td>Module datasheet, host supply, optical connection and interface.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h2>Specify the complete measurement chain</h2>
  <p>Provide the equipment type, measurement-point schedule, temperature envelope, required accuracy and response, installation constraints and plant interface. Confirm values against the selected model datasheet rather than combining specifications from different product families.</p>
  <p>For application planning, review <a href="/solutions/dry-type-transformer-temperature-monitoring/">dry-type transformer monitoring</a> or the <a href="/solutions/transformer-fiber-optic-temperature-monitoring/">transformer monitoring architecture</a>. Start with <a href="/resources/what-is-a-fiber-optic-temperature-sensor/">the sensor overview</a> and <a href="/resources/fiber-optic-temperature-sensor-selection-guide/">sensor selection guide</a> if you are comparing measurement methods.</p>
</div></section><CTA/></Base>
